# face-box.obj - test-only (mods/_unitface): a 0.6-unit box whose FRONT face (+z in the file, the glTF / Blender
# front) is cyan and whose BACK face (-z) is yellow; every other face is magenta. Hand-written for this repo (no game
# data). The colours come from textures/models/face-box.png (16x4: magenta | cyan | yellow | magenta cells), one
# texture coordinate per face (the cell centre), so a face is one flat colour under the mesh shader's Lambert shade.
# The loader mirrors z into the game's axes, so the front ends up on world -z: at face yaw 0 (the unit faces (0,-1))
# the cyan face looks to the lower right of the screen; turned away ((1,0) / (0,1)) the yellow back face shows instead.
# 8 corners, 6 face normals, 3 texture points; 12 triangles, counter-clockwise seen from outside.
o face_box
v -0.3 0.0 -0.3
v  0.3 0.0 -0.3
v  0.3 0.0  0.3
v -0.3 0.0  0.3
v -0.3 0.6 -0.3
v  0.3 0.6 -0.3
v  0.3 0.6  0.3
v -0.3 0.6  0.3
vt 0.125 0.5
vt 0.375 0.5
vt 0.625 0.5
vn  0 -1  0
vn  0  1  0
vn  0  0 -1
vn  0  0  1
vn -1  0  0
vn  1  0  0
# bottom (y = 0, normal -y): magenta
f 1/1/1 2/1/1 3/1/1
f 1/1/1 3/1/1 4/1/1
# top (y = 0.6, normal +y): magenta
f 5/1/2 8/1/2 7/1/2
f 5/1/2 7/1/2 6/1/2
# back (z = -0.3, normal -z): yellow
f 1/3/3 5/3/3 6/3/3
f 1/3/3 6/3/3 2/3/3
# front (z = +0.3, normal +z): cyan
f 4/2/4 3/2/4 7/2/4
f 4/2/4 7/2/4 8/2/4
# left (x = -0.3, normal -x): magenta
f 1/1/5 4/1/5 8/1/5
f 1/1/5 8/1/5 5/1/5
# right (x = +0.3, normal +x): magenta
f 2/1/6 6/1/6 7/1/6
f 2/1/6 7/1/6 3/1/6
